1
00:00:02,135 --> 00:00:03,804
EPISODE 16

2
00:00:04,304 --> 00:00:06,473
What do I do about this now, seriously?

3
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:07,808
We're ruined.

4
00:00:07,875 --> 00:00:10,077
I said we should harvest early, man!

5
00:00:10,143 --> 00:00:11,512
What do we do?

6
00:00:12,679 --> 00:00:14,915
Sir, what should we do about this?

7
00:00:14,982 --> 00:00:17,985
Look at you boys, all scared.
Nothing to be scared of.

8
00:00:18,051 --> 00:00:19,820
You boys can just drink makgeolli

9
00:00:19,887 --> 00:00:22,222
and play some Go-Stop, got it?

10
00:00:23,457 --> 00:00:24,324
Why, sir?

11
00:00:25,158 --> 00:00:27,060
This is called wintering cabbage.

12
00:00:27,127 --> 00:00:29,196
-Wintering cabbage!
-Wintering cabbage?

13
00:00:29,263 --> 00:00:31,999
What's "wintering"?
It means surviving the winter.

14
00:00:32,065 --> 00:00:33,500
Wait for the snow to melt

15
00:00:33,567 --> 00:00:36,069
and have a glass of makgeolli, got it?

16
00:00:36,136 --> 00:00:37,671
I'm off to drink makgeolli…

17
00:00:37,738 --> 00:00:39,439
-Um, sir--
-Play Go-Stop? One Go!

18
00:00:39,506 --> 00:00:40,374
Let's go!

19
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:41,608
-It's on me.
-Sir!

20
00:00:41,675 --> 00:00:42,910
It should be fine.

21
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:45,779
Why do you care about me? Why?

22
00:00:45,846 --> 00:00:47,214
I don't know either.

23
00:00:47,281 --> 00:00:49,316
I have no idea why I care so much

24
00:00:49,383 --> 00:00:51,485
about your expressions, eyes, and tone!

25
00:00:51,552 --> 00:00:53,420
But what can I do when I do care?

26
00:00:54,588 --> 00:00:57,157
You really make me feel miserable
to the very end.

27
00:00:57,224 --> 00:00:58,559
What? What did I do?

28
00:00:58,625 --> 00:01:01,728
The only reason you care about me,

29
00:01:01,795 --> 00:01:03,797
an unwed mom working as Village Head,

30
00:01:03,864 --> 00:01:06,867
is out of pity and sympathy
for your old first love.

31
00:01:07,834 --> 00:01:10,370
-What?
-But I…

32
00:01:10,437 --> 00:01:12,773
I really don't want that kind of pity.

33
00:01:13,540 --> 00:01:15,208
So I'll say this one more time.

34
00:01:15,275 --> 00:01:20,047
Stop caring about my tone,
my eyes, or even my expressions

35
00:01:20,113 --> 00:01:22,516
because it really makes me feel awful.

36
00:01:28,121 --> 00:01:29,957
Why are you like this again?

37
00:01:30,023 --> 00:01:32,359
Did you fight with Yun-hui again?

38
00:01:32,859 --> 00:01:35,362
Why fight with a woman
who means nothing to me?

39
00:01:35,429 --> 00:01:37,631
Jeez, you totally fought.

40
00:01:38,599 --> 00:01:40,300
Mister, wait for me!

41
00:01:43,503 --> 00:01:44,871
Hey.

42
00:01:45,539 --> 00:01:48,775
Let's harvest the cabbage now
and get out of this awful town.

43
00:01:48,842 --> 00:01:51,478
-I'm so sick of this.
-Once cabbage prices soar,

44
00:01:51,545 --> 00:01:53,747
we couldn't even stay. Be patient, man.

45
00:01:53,814 --> 00:01:55,482
I swear, seriously.

46
00:01:57,517 --> 00:01:59,219
Where did Hotteok go?

47
00:02:01,989 --> 00:02:05,993
Hey, Hotteok!
What are you doing out there, punk?

48
00:02:06,059 --> 00:02:08,128
I just gave you a bath yesterday!

49
00:02:08,195 --> 00:02:09,463
Come here, hurry!

50
00:02:09,529 --> 00:02:12,466
Hey, you're so white I can't find you.

51
00:02:13,634 --> 00:02:15,469
Hey! You little punk!

52
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:18,905
Hotteok! Hotteok!

53
00:02:20,073 --> 00:02:22,042
You're getting all filthy, buddy!

54
00:02:22,843 --> 00:02:23,977
Hotteok! What now?

55
00:02:25,245 --> 00:02:27,147
You need a bath right now.

56
00:02:27,214 --> 00:02:29,683
GIRL BOY, BAU'S FAMILY

57
00:02:36,156 --> 00:02:39,026
Hey, is now the time to read comics?

58
00:02:39,092 --> 00:02:40,827
What's the big deal?

59
00:02:40,894 --> 00:02:42,896
Do I stare at a comatose guy all day?

60
00:02:48,068 --> 00:02:50,070
-Watch him closely.
-I'm watching him.

61
00:02:50,137 --> 00:02:51,705
Damn it.

62
00:02:51,772 --> 00:02:53,840
I said, watch him closely.

63
00:02:53,907 --> 00:02:56,009
I'm going to see the Assemblyman.

64
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:01,682
Look at him putting on airs…

65
00:03:01,748 --> 00:03:03,684
I can't stand that obnoxious jerk.

66
00:03:24,004 --> 00:03:28,308
HADUROK-RI

67
00:03:29,743 --> 00:03:35,115
HADUROK-RI RURAL EXPERIENCE VILLAGE

68
00:03:35,182 --> 00:03:37,284
We're here.

69
00:03:37,350 --> 00:03:38,985
It's so nice.

70
00:03:39,653 --> 00:03:41,555
-Gosh, it's nice!
-Welcome, everyone!

71
00:03:41,621 --> 00:03:43,824
-Please come on in.
-Hello.

72
00:03:43,890 --> 00:03:45,092
Hello, everyone.

73
00:03:45,158 --> 00:03:47,861
I'm Kang Yun-hui,
Rural Experience Village Head.

74
00:03:47,928 --> 00:03:49,896
-Yes, hello.
-Hello.

75
00:03:49,963 --> 00:03:52,733
Thank you for coming out to greet us.

76
00:03:52,799 --> 00:03:55,836
It must have been a long, tiring trip.

77
00:03:55,902 --> 00:03:56,837
Not at all, sir.

78
00:03:56,903 --> 00:03:59,573
We had a pleasant trip, like a picnic.

79
00:03:59,639 --> 00:04:02,275
This village is really lovely.

80
00:04:02,342 --> 00:04:04,945
It really is, and the air is so fresh.

81
00:04:05,011 --> 00:04:05,879
Right?

82
00:04:05,946 --> 00:04:06,813
-Yes.

83
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:08,615
I'm so glad to hear that.

84
00:04:08,682 --> 00:04:11,051
Let me show you to your lodging first.

85
00:04:11,118 --> 00:04:12,419
-Follow me.
-Let's go.

86
00:04:12,486 --> 00:04:14,955
-Right this way.
-Yes, okay.

87
00:04:15,021 --> 00:04:16,690
Right here, right here.

88
00:04:17,891 --> 00:04:19,626
Oh my, that looks heavy.

89
00:04:19,693 --> 00:04:21,995
Come on in, come on in.

90
00:04:22,896 --> 00:04:26,199
This is where you'll all be staying.

91
00:04:26,266 --> 00:04:29,136
-It's so cozy and nice.
-Isn't it?

92
00:04:29,202 --> 00:04:31,838
Normally, this is our village hall.

93
00:04:31,905 --> 00:04:35,308
It's built with red clay,
so it's great for kids' eczema.

94
00:04:35,375 --> 00:04:37,177
-Oh, I see.
-Oh, okay.

95
00:04:38,145 --> 00:04:40,147
By the way, what's this basket?

96
00:04:40,213 --> 00:04:41,214
This one?

97
00:04:41,982 --> 00:04:43,183
This is…

98
00:04:43,250 --> 00:04:45,619
our Welcome! Famine-Relief Basket!

99
00:04:46,753 --> 00:04:48,989
A Welcome Famine-Relief Basket?

100
00:04:49,055 --> 00:04:51,525
Yes, you know when you travel abroad…

101
00:04:51,591 --> 00:04:53,426
how hotels welcome you

102
00:04:53,493 --> 00:04:55,695
with a fruit basket right on the bed?

103
00:04:55,762 --> 00:04:57,564
Think of it as something similar.

104
00:04:57,631 --> 00:04:59,599
Oh, okay.

105
00:04:59,666 --> 00:05:01,134
If you need anything,

106
00:05:01,201 --> 00:05:03,904
please feel free to call me anytime.

107
00:05:03,970 --> 00:05:06,173
Well, you have to go pick strawberries.

108
00:05:06,239 --> 00:05:07,374
Unpack and come out.

109
00:05:07,440 --> 00:05:09,276
-Yes, understood.
-Yes, okay.

110
00:05:10,510 --> 00:05:11,812
Let's hurry and unpack!

111
00:05:11,878 --> 00:05:13,580
-Okay!

112
00:05:13,647 --> 00:05:15,982
Huh? Dad, look over there.

113
00:05:16,950 --> 00:05:18,051
Huh?

114
00:05:18,118 --> 00:05:18,985
Oh!

115
00:05:23,123 --> 00:05:24,491
-Wow.
-Oh, my.

116
00:05:24,558 --> 00:05:25,425
My goodness!

117
00:05:25,492 --> 00:05:27,961
Oh, my, every famous person is here.

118
00:05:28,028 --> 00:05:31,298
HADUROK-RI COMMUNITY HALL

119
00:05:31,364 --> 00:05:32,732
Well? Do they like it?

120
00:05:32,799 --> 00:05:34,901
Yes, we're off to a good start.

121
00:05:34,968 --> 00:05:37,470
-Well, that's a relief.
-Yes, it really is.

122
00:05:37,537 --> 00:05:41,041
Word of mouth is so important
for a Rural Experience Village.

123
00:05:41,107 --> 00:05:43,944
We've made a good first impression,

124
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:45,879
so please be careful, very careful,

125
00:05:45,946 --> 00:05:48,148
and never make even a small mistake.

126
00:05:48,215 --> 00:05:50,450
-Is that clear, everyone?
-Sure.

127
00:05:50,517 --> 00:05:52,519
Man-gu, ready for strawberry picking?

128
00:05:52,586 --> 00:05:54,588
What's there to get ready?

129
00:05:54,654 --> 00:05:56,923
I'll do it as usual. Just as usual.

130
00:05:56,990 --> 00:05:59,192
I don't only care when guests are here

131
00:05:59,259 --> 00:06:01,695
and slack off when they're not, right?

132
00:06:01,761 --> 00:06:03,930
Still, please get everything ready.

133
00:06:03,997 --> 00:06:04,965
Okay? Got it?

134
00:06:05,031 --> 00:06:08,168
I told you to drop it. Enough already!

135
00:06:10,337 --> 00:06:12,806
By the way, Ma, where did I-ji go?

136
00:06:12,873 --> 00:06:14,074
She's not home either.

137
00:06:14,140 --> 00:06:16,910
I don't know. I don't think
she came home last night.

138
00:06:16,977 --> 00:06:19,446
You won't open a coffee shop,
so she ran away?

139
00:06:19,512 --> 00:06:21,348
That little brat, I swear!

140
00:06:21,414 --> 00:06:23,984
A strawberry protest,
and now she even ran away?

141
00:06:24,050 --> 00:06:27,120
Fine, let her do whatever she wants.

142
00:06:27,187 --> 00:06:29,756
She thinks that'll make me
open a coffee shop?

143
00:06:29,823 --> 00:06:31,725
Fat chance of that happening.

144
00:06:31,791 --> 00:06:33,960
Just wait till that brat comes home.

145
00:06:34,027 --> 00:06:37,063
You have so much money. Just open one.

146
00:06:45,171 --> 00:06:46,106
He's ice-cold!

147
00:06:46,172 --> 00:06:48,008
Oh, no, what should I do?

148
00:06:48,074 --> 00:06:49,476
At this rate, he'll die!

149
00:06:49,542 --> 00:06:51,411
Oh! Mr. Han!

150
00:06:53,380 --> 00:06:55,749
Please wake up, Mr. Han!

151
00:06:56,449 --> 00:06:59,052
You cannot die like this, Mr. Han.

152
00:06:59,119 --> 00:07:00,954
Please don't leave me behind.

153
00:07:01,021 --> 00:07:02,689
Mr. Han!

154
00:07:10,497 --> 00:07:12,999
Well, I'm busy, so I'll be going.

155
00:07:17,604 --> 00:07:20,373
Sang-deuk, is the cabbage ready
for making kimchi?

156
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:22,409
Yes, don't worry about it.

157
00:07:23,677 --> 00:07:25,312
Sang-deuk!

158
00:07:26,880 --> 00:07:28,982
Bong-ryeon, why are you here again?

159
00:07:29,049 --> 00:07:31,318
I heard you're holding a kimchi event.

160
00:07:31,384 --> 00:07:33,320
So I came to help you out.

161
00:07:34,254 --> 00:07:36,723
Look at this guy getting all shy.

162
00:07:38,258 --> 00:07:39,726
It's not like that at all.

163
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:41,728
I'm losing my mind.

164
00:07:41,795 --> 00:07:43,630
Sang-deuk, where are you going?

165
00:07:43,697 --> 00:07:47,500
I'm so frustrated,
I'm going to get a drink. A drink!

166
00:07:49,769 --> 00:07:51,204
What a shy guy.

167
00:07:51,972 --> 00:07:54,274
Stop playing hard to get, Sang-deuk!

168
00:08:07,754 --> 00:08:09,055
What's with you lately?

169
00:08:09,122 --> 00:08:10,557
What about me?

170
00:08:10,623 --> 00:08:12,659
You seem like a different person.

171
00:08:12,726 --> 00:08:15,195
I don't know what,
but something's different.

172
00:08:15,261 --> 00:08:17,630
Whether I changed or not,
what's it to you?

173
00:08:17,697 --> 00:08:20,600
-Because I care about you!
-I already told you.

174
00:08:21,134 --> 00:08:23,269
Stop caring about Min-ho and me now.

175
00:08:23,336 --> 00:08:25,605
How can I not care when I do?

176
00:08:25,672 --> 00:08:27,841
Why do you care about me? Why?

177
00:08:27,907 --> 00:08:29,275
I don't know either!

178
00:08:29,342 --> 00:08:31,277
Why I care about your look, eyes,

179
00:08:31,344 --> 00:08:33,813
and your every single tone,
even I don't know.

180
00:08:48,561 --> 00:08:51,564
Gosh, that mother-in-law is so mean.

181
00:08:51,631 --> 00:08:53,299
By the way, where is Yun-hui?

182
00:08:53,366 --> 00:08:57,203
The Rural Experience Village guests
are coming today, remember?

183
00:08:57,270 --> 00:08:59,305
Oh, that's today.

184
00:08:59,372 --> 00:09:01,941
She must be swamped. That sounds tough.

185
00:09:02,976 --> 00:09:04,144
Who made her do it?

186
00:09:04,210 --> 00:09:05,945
She started it. She'll manage.

187
00:09:06,846 --> 00:09:09,349
Why are you in such a foul mood lately?

188
00:09:09,416 --> 00:09:11,484
When was I? When?

189
00:09:11,551 --> 00:09:13,119
Package for Yoo Han-cheol!

190
00:09:13,186 --> 00:09:15,055
It's here! Yes, just a moment!

191
00:09:15,989 --> 00:09:17,057
Why a package now?

192
00:09:17,123 --> 00:09:19,426
You fine gentlemen need not know.

193
00:09:22,128 --> 00:09:24,364
Let's not mind it and go to the field.

194
00:09:24,431 --> 00:09:26,800
-Okay.
-Let us be off!

195
00:09:30,203 --> 00:09:33,039
-Yu-na, why are you out?
-Going to the field, right?

196
00:09:33,106 --> 00:09:35,542
-I want to tag along.
-No, you can't.

197
00:09:35,608 --> 00:09:38,478
Rural Experience Village guests
came from Seoul today,

198
00:09:38,545 --> 00:09:39,446
and may spot you.

199
00:09:39,512 --> 00:09:41,281
I just feel so stifled in here.

200
00:09:42,315 --> 00:09:44,317
Then how about a walk this evening?

201
00:09:44,384 --> 00:09:47,287
Even if it's stifling,
be patient during the day, okay?

202
00:09:48,288 --> 00:09:49,556
Okay, I will.

203
00:09:49,622 --> 00:09:51,424
Oh, Yun-hui!

204
00:09:51,491 --> 00:09:53,326
Did the guests arrive safely?

205
00:09:53,393 --> 00:09:54,527
Yes.

206
00:09:55,195 --> 00:09:56,229
Oh, right.

207
00:09:56,296 --> 00:09:59,499
You didn't forget you'll run
the fire-can game later, right?

208
00:09:59,566 --> 00:10:01,901
It's tonight, so get it ready, okay?

209
00:10:01,968 --> 00:10:04,370
Get it ready? What do we even prepare?

210
00:10:04,437 --> 00:10:06,739
You don't know the fire-can game?

211
00:10:06,806 --> 00:10:09,442
Yun-hui, we're like family now,

212
00:10:09,509 --> 00:10:11,444
and not like strangers, I know.

213
00:10:11,511 --> 00:10:13,680
We're Seoul natives, born and raised.

214
00:10:13,746 --> 00:10:15,081
Would we have played it?

215
00:10:15,148 --> 00:10:16,683
That's true.

216
00:10:17,283 --> 00:10:20,053
Right, Min-gi! You know how, right?

217
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:21,955
Lead the guys and get it ready.

218
00:10:22,856 --> 00:10:24,057
Forget it.

219
00:10:24,124 --> 00:10:26,626
You said to stay out of your business.

220
00:10:27,494 --> 00:10:28,795
I'm leaving.

221
00:10:37,370 --> 00:10:38,605
You and Min-gi fought?

222
00:10:38,671 --> 00:10:41,975
Oh, no. We didn't fight or anything.

223
00:10:43,009 --> 00:10:45,678
But how will we do the fire-can game?

224
00:10:45,745 --> 00:10:47,013
Don't worry, I'm here.

225
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:50,817
Gosh, it scares me the most
when you say things like that.

226
00:10:51,751 --> 00:10:55,021
Ki-jun, this won't do. You take charge.

227
00:10:55,088 --> 00:10:57,891
Don't listen to, look at,
or believe Hyeok, got it?

228
00:10:57,957 --> 00:10:59,359
Okay, I'll get it ready.

229
00:10:59,425 --> 00:11:01,961
-We'll head out for now.
-Okay, thanks.

230
00:11:02,028 --> 00:11:03,062
-Rest up.
-Okay.

231
00:11:03,129 --> 00:11:04,864
-I'll be back.
-Okay, good luck.

232
00:11:06,199 --> 00:11:08,968
Oh, my dear Yu-na, did you sleep well?

233
00:11:09,769 --> 00:11:10,937
Yes.

234
00:11:11,471 --> 00:11:13,940
I'm tired, so I'll head back inside.

235
00:11:24,684 --> 00:11:27,820
Man-gu's strawberries!

236
00:11:27,887 --> 00:11:30,623
Sir, please buy some strawberries!

237
00:11:30,690 --> 00:11:34,260
Welcome to Man-gu's Strawberry Farm!

238
00:11:34,327 --> 00:11:36,095
MAN-GU'S OSAM STRAWBERRY FARM

239
00:11:36,162 --> 00:11:38,665
If I may speak of our strawberry farm,

240
00:11:38,731 --> 00:11:41,067
with eco-friendly,
pesticide-free farming,

241
00:11:41,134 --> 00:11:44,637
every year, we boast
astronomical profits.

242
00:11:44,704 --> 00:11:47,373
With a cutting-edge system year-round,

243
00:11:47,440 --> 00:11:50,643
we produce delicious strawberries.

244
00:11:50,710 --> 00:11:51,978
Man-gu's strawberries!

245
00:11:52,045 --> 00:11:53,546
Is that so?

246
00:11:53,613 --> 00:11:57,684
But do you usually
work dressed like that?

247
00:11:57,750 --> 00:12:00,220
Yes, indeed. This is my work uniform.

248
00:12:00,286 --> 00:12:02,722
-Yes. Why, is it strange?
-Oh, no.

249
00:12:02,789 --> 00:12:06,759
Now then, let us officially begin
the strawberry-picking experience.

250
00:12:06,826 --> 00:12:08,061
Please step inside.

251
00:12:08,127 --> 00:12:10,997
-Wow, the strawberries look so good!
-They're the best!

252
00:12:11,664 --> 00:12:14,300
Come on in, everyone. Come right in.

253
00:12:16,236 --> 00:12:17,904
Right here… Oh my goodness!

254
00:12:21,241 --> 00:12:23,476
What are you doing in here?

255
00:12:23,543 --> 00:12:26,913
What? Where did all my strawberries go?

256
00:12:30,416 --> 00:12:32,085
I said I would eat them all.

257
00:12:32,151 --> 00:12:37,056
What? Did you really pick and eat
all the strawberries in here?

258
00:12:37,123 --> 00:12:40,593
While I'm still being nice,
open a coffee shop for me! Open one!

259
00:12:40,660 --> 00:12:43,630
This crazy girl! Why, I ought to just…

260
00:12:44,764 --> 00:12:48,668
Oh dear, I am told the strawberries
in here have all been shipped out.

261
00:12:48,735 --> 00:12:50,436
However, please do not worry.

262
00:12:50,503 --> 00:12:52,071
Right in the next greenhouse,

263
00:12:52,138 --> 00:12:54,173
even more strawberries await us.

264
00:12:54,240 --> 00:12:55,875
Please follow me. Follow…

265
00:12:57,343 --> 00:12:59,445
More berries are next door. This way!

266
00:12:59,512 --> 00:13:01,614
Yes, yes, please go right in.

267
00:13:02,181 --> 00:13:04,284
Here we are, yes. The strawberries.

268
00:13:04,350 --> 00:13:06,252
Come right on in, please. Yes.

269
00:13:06,319 --> 00:13:07,720
Now, prepare yourselves!

270
00:13:07,787 --> 00:13:09,922
Step right on in, everyone.

271
00:13:09,989 --> 00:13:14,193
The strawberries here are much plumper
than the ones over there, and…

272
00:13:16,095 --> 00:13:18,598
What is this? How did this…

273
00:13:18,665 --> 00:13:20,500
Where did all my strawberries go?

274
00:13:26,939 --> 00:13:29,208
What? Then don't tell me…

275
00:13:29,275 --> 00:13:32,545
you picked and ate
all the strawberries here too?

276
00:13:33,546 --> 00:13:37,016
So hurry up and open that coffee shop.

277
00:13:37,083 --> 00:13:39,452
You've lost your mind, you crazy girl!

278
00:13:39,519 --> 00:13:42,255
How many strawberries did you gorge on?

279
00:13:42,322 --> 00:13:45,458
You and I both die today!
Get over here, you brat!

280
00:13:45,525 --> 00:13:47,760
-Get out here!
-The kids are watching…

281
00:13:47,827 --> 00:13:50,396
You brat! Get out here!
You and I both die!

282
00:13:50,463 --> 00:13:52,265
Do you have any sense or not?

283
00:13:52,332 --> 00:13:54,467
Excuse me, sir! Sir!

284
00:13:54,534 --> 00:13:58,137
Calm down! You'll kill your daughter!

285
00:13:58,204 --> 00:14:00,440
Daughter? My daughter? My daughter?

286
00:14:00,506 --> 00:14:03,543
She's my younger sister!
Can't you tell by looking?

287
00:14:03,609 --> 00:14:05,411
You crazy brat, come over here!

288
00:14:05,478 --> 00:14:07,780
-When will you wise up?
-What's wrong?

289
00:14:07,847 --> 00:14:10,516
I-ji, what's wrong? What is this?

290
00:14:10,583 --> 00:14:13,986
You came just in time.
Please stop your husband.

291
00:14:14,053 --> 00:14:15,855
What, her husband? Her husband?

292
00:14:15,922 --> 00:14:17,156
She's my mom! My mom!

293
00:14:17,223 --> 00:14:19,092
Can't you tell? Can't you see that?

294
00:14:19,158 --> 00:14:20,693
Uh… He says she's his mom.

295
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:22,962
Oh my, what? What's going on here?

296
00:14:23,029 --> 00:14:25,331
I'm so sorry. Oh dear, I'm so sorry.

297
00:14:25,398 --> 00:14:27,667
I don't even know how to apologize.

298
00:14:28,468 --> 00:14:30,670
The strawberry tour had a small mishap,

299
00:14:30,737 --> 00:14:33,706
but this will never happen again.

300
00:14:33,773 --> 00:14:36,008
May I ask for your understanding?

301
00:14:36,075 --> 00:14:38,077
No, it's totally fine.

302
00:14:38,144 --> 00:14:39,312
Don't worry about it.

303
00:14:39,379 --> 00:14:42,148
Thank you so much for understanding.

304
00:14:42,882 --> 00:14:46,919
Next up, for tomorrow morning's
kimchi-making session,

305
00:14:46,986 --> 00:14:49,389
let's go try salting cabbages.

306
00:14:49,455 --> 00:14:50,423
Come this way.

307
00:14:50,490 --> 00:14:52,925
Okay, let's go, let's go.

308
00:14:56,863 --> 00:15:01,300
You have to flip the cabbages halfway
like this so they get salted evenly.

309
00:15:02,568 --> 00:15:04,070
It's fun, right, kids?

310
00:15:04,137 --> 00:15:06,305
Yes, but it's hard.

311
00:15:06,372 --> 00:15:07,373
Me too.

312
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:10,109
Since making kimchi is this hard,

313
00:15:10,176 --> 00:15:12,912
eat more kimchi and stop fussing
over side dishes.

314
00:15:12,979 --> 00:15:14,647
-Okay.

315
00:15:14,714 --> 00:15:16,716
That's so nice to see.

316
00:15:16,783 --> 00:15:21,120
My dream is to have one son
and one daughter someday too…

317
00:15:23,156 --> 00:15:25,191
She sure has a unique laugh.

318
00:15:26,893 --> 00:15:28,628
But who is that lady?

319
00:15:28,694 --> 00:15:32,064
She's my grandson's bride-to-be.

320
00:15:32,131 --> 00:15:34,767
You see, she likes my grandson so much

321
00:15:34,834 --> 00:15:38,004
that she comes every day to help out.

322
00:15:38,838 --> 00:15:41,974
My, your grandson must be so handsome.

323
00:15:44,444 --> 00:15:46,712
I'm so thirsty. So thirsty.

324
00:15:53,853 --> 00:15:55,755
By any chance, is he…

325
00:15:55,822 --> 00:15:58,758
Yes, that's my grandson.

326
00:16:13,506 --> 00:16:15,475
By the way, isn't he eating?

327
00:16:15,541 --> 00:16:19,312
Cold, so cold. My noggin is freezing!

328
00:16:19,979 --> 00:16:22,315
Don't mind him. Please eat.

329
00:16:22,381 --> 00:16:25,117
He does that every other day.

330
00:16:27,353 --> 00:16:29,489
He just really likes to drink,

331
00:16:29,555 --> 00:16:32,825
but he's a very kind and innocent guy.

332
00:16:32,892 --> 00:16:35,228
-Oh, I see.
-Right.

333
00:16:36,762 --> 00:16:38,297
Oh? Those are almonds.

334
00:16:38,364 --> 00:16:40,933
Why? Do you want some?

335
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:43,870
What? Really? I really love almonds!

336
00:16:43,936 --> 00:16:47,607
Then take them all
and eat them when you get hungry.

337
00:16:47,673 --> 00:16:49,375
Thank you so much.

338
00:16:49,442 --> 00:16:52,378
Don't eat it, don't eat it!
You'll be in big trouble!

339
00:16:55,281 --> 00:16:58,518
He means don't drink alcohol,
since the kids are here.

340
00:16:59,519 --> 00:17:02,188
Please eat. Just eat comfortably.

341
00:17:02,255 --> 00:17:04,023
Want some side dishes?

342
00:17:04,090 --> 00:17:06,092
How long do I have to do this crap?

343
00:17:06,158 --> 00:17:08,794
Where on earth is the money, huh?

344
00:17:08,861 --> 00:17:11,831
We dug up every possible spot,
and it's not here!

345
00:17:11,898 --> 00:17:14,033
Still, we can't give up now, can we?

346
00:17:14,100 --> 00:17:16,736
-Exactly.
-This is driving me crazy, darn it.

347
00:17:16,802 --> 00:17:18,404
Su-yeon!

348
00:17:18,971 --> 00:17:20,072
Su-yeon!

349
00:17:23,209 --> 00:17:24,777
Why are you so startled?

350
00:17:24,844 --> 00:17:26,612
Han-cheol, what is it this time?

351
00:17:26,679 --> 00:17:29,782
Um, do you have some time tomorrow?

352
00:17:29,849 --> 00:17:31,317
No, I don't.

353
00:17:31,384 --> 00:17:34,020
Come on, please make some time for me.

354
00:17:34,086 --> 00:17:37,256
It's about something really important.

355
00:17:37,323 --> 00:17:38,958
What is it?

356
00:17:39,025 --> 00:17:40,359
I'll tell you tomorrow.

357
00:17:42,295 --> 00:17:45,131
Um, I'm not in the mood right now.

358
00:17:45,197 --> 00:17:46,933
I have no time. What can I do?

359
00:17:50,236 --> 00:17:51,504
Is that so?

360
00:17:52,638 --> 00:17:54,840
Then I guess there's nothing I can do.

361
00:18:05,017 --> 00:18:07,119
Gosh, this is driving me crazy!

362
00:18:13,259 --> 00:18:15,561
Um, Han-cheol!

363
00:18:15,628 --> 00:18:16,896
Yes?

364
00:18:17,830 --> 00:18:21,133
When and where do we meet tomorrow?

365
00:18:22,401 --> 00:18:23,869
So you'll make time for me?

366
00:18:23,936 --> 00:18:27,106
Here at the bus stop tomorrow by nine.

367
00:18:27,173 --> 00:18:29,008
See you by 9:00 a.m., okay?

368
00:18:29,075 --> 00:18:30,309
Thank you!

369
00:18:35,781 --> 00:18:37,049
What's with you?

370
00:18:37,116 --> 00:18:40,686
Is this the time to date that guy?

371
00:18:40,753 --> 00:18:43,189
A… a date? It's not a date!

372
00:18:43,856 --> 00:18:45,424
You're acting weird.

373
00:18:45,491 --> 00:18:48,361
Do you actually like that guy?

374
00:18:48,427 --> 00:18:50,730
Come on! What are you talking about?

375
00:18:50,796 --> 00:18:53,299
I pity his life, that's why!
I just pity him!

376
00:18:53,366 --> 00:18:55,601
Jeez, I'll find the money
and skip town.

377
00:18:55,668 --> 00:18:57,637
I really can't take this anymore!

378
00:18:58,638 --> 00:19:00,306
She's acting weird.

379
00:19:02,208 --> 00:19:04,310
Seriously, nothing's going right today.

380
00:19:04,377 --> 00:19:06,278
Not a single thing, jeez.

381
00:19:08,714 --> 00:19:10,883
Huh? What are you two doing there?

382
00:19:13,986 --> 00:19:16,522
-Oh, prepping for the fire-can game?
-Yes.

383
00:19:16,589 --> 00:19:18,324
Let me see, let me see.

384
00:19:18,391 --> 00:19:19,859
Ta-da!

385
00:19:22,795 --> 00:19:24,697
Gosh, this thing is way too small.

386
00:19:24,764 --> 00:19:26,599
How do we spin fire in this?

387
00:19:26,666 --> 00:19:27,967
This tiny thing, damn it!

388
00:19:28,034 --> 00:19:29,301
Right? A bit small, huh?

389
00:19:29,902 --> 00:19:32,705
It should be this size
for the fire-can game, right?

390
00:19:32,772 --> 00:19:35,841
This one is an awkwardly big size.

391
00:19:35,908 --> 00:19:38,344
-It's just awkward.
-It's too big?

392
00:19:38,411 --> 00:19:40,212
We can't use Han-cheol's either.

393
00:19:40,279 --> 00:19:41,614
Han-cheol's?

394
00:19:48,087 --> 00:19:50,489
Ugh, you dumb ox of a bastard!

395
00:19:50,556 --> 00:19:53,993
It's way too big!
Do you want to burn the village down?

396
00:19:54,060 --> 00:19:56,896
You'll dislocate your arm
spinning this, you idiot!

397
00:19:56,962 --> 00:19:59,098
Gosh, these little bastards, I swear!

398
00:19:59,165 --> 00:20:01,834
I'm a total idiot
for leaving this to you two!

399
00:20:01,901 --> 00:20:03,536
I'm just a total idiot!

400
00:20:04,103 --> 00:20:07,306
It's almost time for the activity.
We're in big trouble!

401
00:20:08,107 --> 00:20:09,842
Gosh, seriously.

402
00:20:12,545 --> 00:20:15,047
-Min-gi.
-Yes?

403
00:20:16,682 --> 00:20:18,718
Let's go for a walk. You promised.

404
00:20:18,784 --> 00:20:20,653
Oh… Right.

405
00:20:25,224 --> 00:20:26,859
Let's go.

406
00:20:26,926 --> 00:20:28,327
Let's go.

407
00:20:35,401 --> 00:20:36,736
Gosh, this won't do.

408
00:20:36,802 --> 00:20:38,571
I'll have to make this myself.

409
00:20:38,637 --> 00:20:39,805
I'm sorry.

410
00:20:39,872 --> 00:20:42,341
How about we take Min-ho with us later?

411
00:20:42,408 --> 00:20:43,642
I think he'd love it.

412
00:20:43,709 --> 00:20:45,644
Should we?

413
00:20:49,148 --> 00:20:51,484
2014 LEE HYEON-SEOK PIANO RECITAL

414
00:20:52,084 --> 00:20:53,719
Min-ho.

415
00:20:57,723 --> 00:20:59,191
Min-ho, what were you doing?

416
00:21:00,059 --> 00:21:02,094
What are you doing at my desk?

417
00:21:02,762 --> 00:21:04,597
I was just looking for an eraser.

418
00:21:04,663 --> 00:21:06,365
Oh, were you?

419
00:21:06,432 --> 00:21:07,566
Oh, right, Min-ho.

420
00:21:07,633 --> 00:21:09,668
I'm going to spin fire cans. Join me?

421
00:21:09,735 --> 00:21:12,972
No, I can't. I have a lot of homework.

422
00:21:13,038 --> 00:21:16,041
Oh, really? It can't be helped, then.

423
00:21:16,108 --> 00:21:18,978
Okay, then. Work hard on your homework.

424
00:21:40,266 --> 00:21:42,368
LEE HYEON-SEOK, PIANIST

425
00:21:46,172 --> 00:21:48,340
Here, watch this. Like this.

426
00:21:48,407 --> 00:21:50,843
You spin it around, whoosh, whoosh!

427
00:21:57,082 --> 00:21:58,317
Isn't this fun?

428
00:21:58,384 --> 00:22:00,186
-Yes!

429
00:22:00,252 --> 00:22:04,356
Originally, in the first lunar month,
people set fire to field ridges

430
00:22:04,423 --> 00:22:06,325
to drive away mice and burn weeds,

431
00:22:06,392 --> 00:22:08,394
reducing damage from pests.

432
00:22:08,460 --> 00:22:10,996
Now, it's evolved into this folk game

433
00:22:11,063 --> 00:22:12,631
of spinning fire in cans.

434
00:22:12,698 --> 00:22:14,834
Oh, I see.

435
00:22:14,900 --> 00:22:17,736
Now, I'll show you
the highlight of this game,

436
00:22:17,803 --> 00:22:20,539
so watch real close and follow along.

437
00:22:20,606 --> 00:22:21,774
The highlight?

438
00:22:21,841 --> 00:22:23,976
Yes, watch closely.

439
00:22:38,290 --> 00:22:41,827
And while watching that, make a wish.

440
00:22:41,894 --> 00:22:43,863
We make wishes spinning fire cans too?

441
00:22:43,929 --> 00:22:48,133
Oh, be quiet.
It just seems meaningful and nice.

442
00:22:50,436 --> 00:22:52,738
And besides, who knows?

443
00:22:52,805 --> 00:22:55,274
Our wishes might really come true.

444
00:23:10,122 --> 00:23:12,358
-Make a wish.

445
00:23:23,636 --> 00:23:25,804
Please just let me live a long life.

446
00:23:29,241 --> 00:23:30,910
Oh, it's hot!

447
00:23:32,711 --> 00:23:35,281
-Oh, it's so hot!
-Eat slowly.

448
00:23:35,347 --> 00:23:37,149
But it's so good!

449
00:23:37,216 --> 00:23:39,218
See? Aren't you glad we came?

450
00:23:39,285 --> 00:23:40,753
-Yes!

451
00:23:54,833 --> 00:23:56,135
-One bite.
-Is it good?

452
00:23:56,201 --> 00:23:57,436
Yes.

453
00:23:57,503 --> 00:24:00,372
What are you staring at so intently?

454
00:24:00,439 --> 00:24:01,573
Huh?

455
00:24:02,541 --> 00:24:04,443
They just look so nice.

456
00:24:06,245 --> 00:24:07,880
Do you envy them?

457
00:24:09,348 --> 00:24:10,816
A little.

458
00:24:10,883 --> 00:24:14,486
Anyway, what did you wish for earlier?

459
00:24:14,553 --> 00:24:16,188
Me?

460
00:24:17,022 --> 00:24:19,258
I just wished for my Min-ho

461
00:24:19,325 --> 00:24:22,528
to grow up healthy and strong.

462
00:24:22,594 --> 00:24:24,630
-What about you?
-Me?

463
00:24:25,297 --> 00:24:27,232
Hmm…

464
00:24:27,299 --> 00:24:31,103
I wished for you to be happy.

465
00:24:31,170 --> 00:24:32,304
What?

466
00:24:32,371 --> 00:24:35,341
Your wish is for me to be happy?

467
00:24:36,408 --> 00:24:37,710
Give me a break.

468
00:24:37,776 --> 00:24:40,646
Hey, I'm plenty happy right now.

469
00:24:41,413 --> 00:24:43,015
Yun-hui.

470
00:24:43,082 --> 00:24:46,051
Even if only sometimes,
lean on me when it gets hard.

471
00:24:46,118 --> 00:24:48,554
Gosh, what are you talking about?

472
00:24:48,620 --> 00:24:50,723
Why would I lean on you?

473
00:24:51,824 --> 00:24:53,525
You never know if someday

474
00:24:53,592 --> 00:24:55,194
you'll want someone to lean on

475
00:24:55,260 --> 00:24:57,663
but have no one to lean on.

476
00:24:57,730 --> 00:24:59,365
And don't try so hard.

477
00:24:59,431 --> 00:25:02,768
Some things just don't work out,
no matter how hard you try.

478
00:25:04,036 --> 00:25:06,271
Who says I'm trying so hard?

479
00:25:07,272 --> 00:25:11,110
I know exactly how you feel.
I'm in the same boat as you.

480
00:25:12,745 --> 00:25:15,147
I have no idea what you're saying.

481
00:25:15,214 --> 00:25:17,349
I'm completely fine.

482
00:25:19,084 --> 00:25:22,287
You're so obvious when you lie.

483
00:25:23,155 --> 00:25:24,890
-I am?
-Yes.

484
00:25:24,957 --> 00:25:26,658
Whenever you tell a lie,

485
00:25:26,725 --> 00:25:30,162
this spot under your nose twitches.

486
00:25:32,498 --> 00:25:34,566
-Do I really do that?
-Yes.

487
00:25:34,633 --> 00:25:39,171
And you get a wrinkle
right here between your eyebrows.

488
00:25:40,973 --> 00:25:42,641
Really?

489
00:25:47,112 --> 00:25:49,481
-What? Why are you laughing?
-Huh?

490
00:25:53,052 --> 00:25:56,889
Why, you! You little brat!

491
00:25:56,955 --> 00:25:57,990
Stop right there!

492
00:25:58,057 --> 00:25:59,858
That little brat, I swear!

493
00:26:03,896 --> 00:26:05,497
Hey! Stop right there!

494
00:26:12,004 --> 00:26:15,707
I felt so cooped up,
but it's much better being outside.

495
00:26:16,875 --> 00:26:19,545
It's gotten so chilly, right, Min-gi?

496
00:26:23,515 --> 00:26:25,284
Min-gi.

497
00:26:27,586 --> 00:26:30,756
-Huh?
-What are you thinking so hard about?

498
00:26:32,224 --> 00:26:34,226
It's because of Yun-hui.

499
00:26:34,293 --> 00:26:36,261
I don't get why she's like this to me.

500
00:26:36,328 --> 00:26:38,564
She's just impossible to figure out.

501
00:26:39,998 --> 00:26:42,501
Why is she so upset
I was nice to Min-ho?

502
00:26:43,335 --> 00:26:44,770
-Min-gi.
-What?

503
00:26:47,106 --> 00:26:49,274
Can you stop mentioning Yun-hui
around me?

504
00:26:49,341 --> 00:26:50,609
What?

505
00:26:52,010 --> 00:26:54,413
I'm sorry.

506
00:26:54,480 --> 00:26:56,415
I'm tired. Let's go inside.

507
00:27:04,289 --> 00:27:06,658
I-ji, why are you acting like this?

508
00:27:06,725 --> 00:27:08,227
What are you, a teenager?

509
00:27:08,293 --> 00:27:09,895
Running away at your age?

510
00:27:11,063 --> 00:27:12,865
I'm independent, not running away.

511
00:27:12,931 --> 00:27:14,233
Independent, my foot!

512
00:27:14,299 --> 00:27:17,603
Your brother won't fund a coffee shop,
so you're protesting.

513
00:27:17,669 --> 00:27:19,104
That's not it.

514
00:27:19,171 --> 00:27:21,140
I've been living too irresponsibly.

515
00:27:21,206 --> 00:27:23,075
I get why my brother doubts me.

516
00:27:23,142 --> 00:27:25,477
This time, I'll do something on my own.

517
00:27:26,111 --> 00:27:27,813
So don't worry, Mom.

518
00:27:27,880 --> 00:27:30,516
Do you even have a place to sleep
at this hour?

519
00:27:30,582 --> 00:27:33,051
I can stay at Mi-yeong's shop.

520
00:27:33,118 --> 00:27:34,186
Don't worry.

521
00:27:35,154 --> 00:27:36,288
I'll go now, Mom.

522
00:27:36,355 --> 00:27:37,723
Come on, I-ji!

523
00:27:37,789 --> 00:27:40,025
Gosh, she's so immature! What do I do?

524
00:27:40,092 --> 00:27:42,961
I'm so upset because of her, really.

525
00:27:43,795 --> 00:27:45,397
Mrs. Kim.

526
00:27:46,798 --> 00:27:48,901
Yes, um… Hello.

527
00:27:48,967 --> 00:27:50,369
I'm busy, so I must go.

528
00:27:50,435 --> 00:27:52,237
-Um, one moment, Mrs. Kim.
-Yes?

529
00:27:52,304 --> 00:27:55,707
Why have you been like this lately?
Did I make some mistake?

530
00:27:55,774 --> 00:27:57,376
No, it's nothing like that.

531
00:27:57,442 --> 00:28:00,379
Then why do you keep avoiding me?

532
00:28:00,445 --> 00:28:02,681
Is it over what happened the other day?

533
00:28:02,748 --> 00:28:06,351
Um, Mr. Han, what happened
the other day…

534
00:28:06,418 --> 00:28:09,421
was just an accident and meant nothing.

535
00:28:09,488 --> 00:28:11,924
So please forget about it, alright?

536
00:28:11,990 --> 00:28:15,561
Please don't get any strange ideas.

537
00:28:15,627 --> 00:28:17,496
Well then, I must go.

538
00:28:17,563 --> 00:28:19,998
-I'm disappointed.
-Pardon?

539
00:28:20,065 --> 00:28:23,669
I thought you felt the same way I did.

540
00:28:24,736 --> 00:28:26,471
But I guess you don't…

541
00:28:27,272 --> 00:28:28,807
Felt the same way?

542
00:28:28,874 --> 00:28:32,144
Since that day, I kept thinking of you.

543
00:28:32,211 --> 00:28:35,113
And every time, my heart fluttered.

544
00:28:38,984 --> 00:28:42,387
But I suppose it was all in my head.

545
00:28:42,955 --> 00:28:45,357
I apologize. I must go then.

546
00:28:46,491 --> 00:28:48,827
Um, Mr. Han!

547
00:28:50,128 --> 00:28:52,531
Yes? What is it?

548
00:28:53,899 --> 00:28:55,867
Actually, I felt the same way too.

549
00:28:55,934 --> 00:28:58,837
Whenever I thought of you,
my heart raced and fluttered.

550
00:28:58,904 --> 00:29:03,008
But I was so embarrassed and shy
that I just…

551
00:29:03,075 --> 00:29:05,043
Is that so?

552
00:29:06,378 --> 00:29:08,113
That's a relief.

553
00:29:15,120 --> 00:29:17,189
Dad! What are you doing here?

554
00:29:17,256 --> 00:29:18,690
Huh? Oh, uh…

555
00:29:23,228 --> 00:29:27,165
Dad, what are you doing with her?

556
00:29:28,133 --> 00:29:30,669
-This is suspicious.
-Suspicious? No way.

557
00:29:31,603 --> 00:29:35,207
Did you eat? You haven't, right?
Let's go get something to eat.

558
00:29:35,274 --> 00:29:37,542
I already ate! I said I ate.

559
00:29:44,149 --> 00:29:47,419
CABBAGE MARKET PRICES PLUNGE

560
00:29:49,388 --> 00:29:51,123
1,500 won a head?

561
00:29:51,189 --> 00:29:53,392
Did the price drop again?

562
00:29:54,159 --> 00:29:56,228
It's been dropping for days.

563
00:29:56,295 --> 00:29:58,597
I have a bad feeling about this.

564
00:29:59,331 --> 00:30:01,199
Don't worry, you punks.

565
00:30:01,266 --> 00:30:05,103
Stocks hit rock bottom,
then bam, they skyrocket!

566
00:30:05,170 --> 00:30:07,039
It's the same thing.

567
00:30:07,105 --> 00:30:08,740
So don't worry about it.

568
00:30:10,242 --> 00:30:11,810
Excuse me, ma'am.

569
00:30:11,877 --> 00:30:13,011
Um, where's Yu-na?

570
00:30:13,078 --> 00:30:16,214
I don't know. She's been
in her room all day. Tired, maybe.

571
00:30:16,281 --> 00:30:17,949
Is that right?

572
00:30:25,791 --> 00:30:27,693
What? What are you bringing in now?

573
00:30:27,759 --> 00:30:29,961
I have somewhere to go today.

574
00:30:30,028 --> 00:30:31,863
You have to go to the field alone.

575
00:30:31,930 --> 00:30:33,999
Where are you going again?

576
00:30:34,066 --> 00:30:35,200
Secret. Top secret.

577
00:30:35,267 --> 00:30:37,936
Sorry, I'll explain it all
when I get back. Bye!

578
00:30:38,003 --> 00:30:40,806
He's slacking off again, darn it!

579
00:30:43,008 --> 00:30:45,010
Oh no, we're late, late, late!

580
00:30:45,077 --> 00:30:47,112
We're late, Min-ho. I'll take you.

581
00:30:47,179 --> 00:30:50,849
-Mom, I'll go by myself today.
-Huh?

582
00:30:50,916 --> 00:30:51,883
Why?

583
00:30:51,950 --> 00:30:55,253
Well, you've been busy lately, Mom.

584
00:30:55,320 --> 00:30:56,988
I'll go on my own.

585
00:30:57,055 --> 00:31:00,692
Aw, my boy is all grown up,
looking out for me like that.

586
00:31:00,759 --> 00:31:03,061
I'll get going then, Mom.

587
00:31:04,129 --> 00:31:05,263
Okay, take care.

588
00:31:05,330 --> 00:31:07,599
-Goodbye!
-Okay.

589
00:31:07,666 --> 00:31:09,701
-Say bye to Grandma too.
-Goodbye!

590
00:31:09,768 --> 00:31:12,704
Okay, Min-ho.
Be careful and have a good day.

591
00:31:12,771 --> 00:31:14,806
Have a good day, my sweet boy.

592
00:31:21,646 --> 00:31:23,315
Please hurry up a little.

593
00:31:23,382 --> 00:31:26,518
Quit rushing me.
My stomach's so upset, I could die.

594
00:31:26,585 --> 00:31:30,021
No one told you to guzzle alcohol.

595
00:31:30,088 --> 00:31:32,224
You've been drinking much more lately.

596
00:31:32,290 --> 00:31:33,658
Is something going on?

597
00:31:33,725 --> 00:31:35,494
No, nothing like that.

598
00:31:36,194 --> 00:31:37,629
Dad! Dad!

599
00:31:37,696 --> 00:31:39,598
What's wrong? What happened?

600
00:31:39,664 --> 00:31:40,832
Yun-hui, what do I do?

601
00:31:40,899 --> 00:31:42,634
Dad was gone when I woke up.

602
00:31:42,701 --> 00:31:44,669
What do you mean? Your dad's gone?

603
00:31:44,736 --> 00:31:47,572
He did that sometimes back in Seoul.

604
00:31:47,639 --> 00:31:50,442
And he almost got in a car accident.

605
00:31:50,509 --> 00:31:51,443
What do I do?

606
00:31:51,510 --> 00:31:53,478
Everything will be fine.

607
00:31:53,545 --> 00:31:55,013
Did you check the village?

608
00:31:55,080 --> 00:31:58,383
Yes, and he's nowhere to be found.

609
00:31:58,450 --> 00:31:59,785
What if he's not okay?

610
00:31:59,851 --> 00:32:02,120
He'll be fine. Don't worry.

611
00:32:02,187 --> 00:32:03,488
I'll help you look.

612
00:32:03,555 --> 00:32:06,158
No, Yun-hui, you stay here. I'll go.

613
00:32:06,224 --> 00:32:07,426
You're on kimchi duty.

614
00:32:07,492 --> 00:32:09,594
Oh, that's right.

615
00:32:09,661 --> 00:32:12,864
Then please go with her and find him.

616
00:32:12,931 --> 00:32:14,466
Go on, hurry.

617
00:32:14,533 --> 00:32:17,035
Why are you standing there? Follow me.

618
00:32:19,371 --> 00:32:21,406
-Sir!
-Dad!

619
00:32:22,140 --> 00:32:24,075
-Sir!
-Dad!

620
00:32:25,444 --> 00:32:26,812
Dad!

621
00:32:26,878 --> 00:32:28,814
I hope nothing happened to him.

622
00:32:38,990 --> 00:32:42,260
Bus to Dong Seoul, one seat left.
Board now for Dong Seoul.

623
00:32:45,197 --> 00:32:47,532
Please have your tickets ready.

624
00:32:55,340 --> 00:32:57,008
Ticket.

625
00:33:01,046 --> 00:33:04,182
Mister, does this bus go to Seoul?

626
00:33:04,249 --> 00:33:05,817
Yes.

627
00:33:05,884 --> 00:33:09,287
Are you traveling alone, kiddo?

628
00:33:09,354 --> 00:33:10,989
Yes, sir.

629
00:33:20,065 --> 00:33:24,236
HADUROK-RI BUS STOP

630
00:33:24,302 --> 00:33:26,738
This is truly the last time. The last.

631
00:33:26,805 --> 00:33:29,040
Don't let that guy sway you, Su-yeon.

632
00:33:30,108 --> 00:33:31,776
Su-yeon!

633
00:33:32,310 --> 00:33:33,912
Su-yeon!

634
00:33:39,117 --> 00:33:40,585
Su-yeon… I'm sorry.

635
00:33:40,652 --> 00:33:41,786
I'm late, aren't I?

636
00:33:41,853 --> 00:33:44,155
No, it's fine.

637
00:33:44,222 --> 00:33:45,657
So where are we going?

638
00:33:45,724 --> 00:33:48,226
You'll see when we get there.

639
00:33:48,994 --> 00:33:51,429
-What are all these boxes?
-These?

640
00:33:51,496 --> 00:33:54,566
Well, you see, these are… a secret!

641
00:33:59,204 --> 00:34:01,039
Dad!

642
00:34:01,106 --> 00:34:03,608
-Sir!
-Dad!

643
00:34:04,376 --> 00:34:05,644
Dad!

644
00:34:05,710 --> 00:34:08,013
Where on earth did he go?

645
00:34:08,079 --> 00:34:09,281
He's not even well.

646
00:34:10,048 --> 00:34:11,449
What am I going to do?

647
00:34:11,516 --> 00:34:14,519
Dad didn't get in an accident, did he?

648
00:34:14,586 --> 00:34:16,221
An accident? No way.

649
00:34:16,288 --> 00:34:18,590
He'll be fine, so don't worry.

650
00:34:19,558 --> 00:34:21,159
Sir!

651
00:34:21,226 --> 00:34:22,227
Dad!

652
00:34:22,961 --> 00:34:25,397
-Sir!
-Dad!

653
00:34:27,332 --> 00:34:29,200
Isn't that him over there?

654
00:34:34,906 --> 00:34:37,275
-Dad!
-Sir!

655
00:34:37,342 --> 00:34:38,977
He's slacking off again.

656
00:34:40,145 --> 00:34:42,314
Let him be. There's not much to do.

657
00:34:42,380 --> 00:34:44,482
Hello there, sister-in-law.

658
00:34:45,016 --> 00:34:46,585
Hi, where are you going?

659
00:34:46,651 --> 00:34:49,454
-I am going to gather mountain herbs.
-In this cold?

660
00:34:49,521 --> 00:34:52,157
To pay Mother's hospital bills,
I have no choice.

661
00:34:53,091 --> 00:34:55,126
I will be on my way, then.

662
00:34:59,898 --> 00:35:01,633
I feel bad for her, too.

663
00:35:01,700 --> 00:35:03,835
If only we had some money to help her.

664
00:35:03,902 --> 00:35:05,670
I know.

665
00:35:05,737 --> 00:35:08,740
Ki-jun, as her husband,
are you just going to stand by?

666
00:35:08,807 --> 00:35:12,711
What do you mean, husband?
Let's just get to work. Hurry.

667
00:35:13,645 --> 00:35:15,947
What a heartless guy.

668
00:35:16,014 --> 00:35:17,682
Hey.

669
00:35:17,749 --> 00:35:19,618
-How long will you do this?
-What?

670
00:35:19,684 --> 00:35:22,153
How long will you be so petty to her?

671
00:35:22,220 --> 00:35:23,822
Cut it out already.

672
00:35:23,888 --> 00:35:26,791
She said she hates me caring
since it feels like pity.

673
00:35:26,858 --> 00:35:28,460
Ever thought why she did that?

674
00:35:28,526 --> 00:35:31,363
-What?
-Forget it. I'm glad you haven't.

675
00:35:31,429 --> 00:35:32,530
What do you mean?

676
00:35:32,597 --> 00:35:35,400
I hope you never, ever figure it out.

677
00:35:35,467 --> 00:35:37,402
That way, I'll have a chance too.

678
00:35:41,206 --> 00:35:44,609
Why does he have to talk in riddles?

679
00:35:44,676 --> 00:35:46,678
She's already bugging me to death.

680
00:35:47,479 --> 00:35:50,315
Why do I keep thinking about her?

681
00:35:51,816 --> 00:35:53,618
Forget it, darn it.

682
00:36:07,966 --> 00:36:11,403
Ki-jun? What brings you here?

683
00:36:11,469 --> 00:36:15,140
Um… I just had nothing much to do.

684
00:36:15,206 --> 00:36:16,941
I came to help you pick herbs.

685
00:36:17,842 --> 00:36:19,044
You didn't have to…

686
00:36:19,911 --> 00:36:21,346
Don't get the wrong idea.

687
00:36:21,413 --> 00:36:25,250
I only came out of curiosity
about the ecology of our wild herbs.

688
00:36:25,316 --> 00:36:27,285
I didn't come because I like you.

689
00:36:27,352 --> 00:36:29,020
Yes, I understand.

690
00:36:29,087 --> 00:36:30,789
Anything to dig up, though?

691
00:36:35,226 --> 00:36:36,594
Aren't your hands cold?

692
00:36:36,661 --> 00:36:38,363
With bare hands and no gloves…

693
00:36:38,430 --> 00:36:39,564
I am fine.

694
00:36:39,631 --> 00:36:41,499
You're not fine at all.

695
00:36:41,566 --> 00:36:43,735
Hurry and put these on for now.

696
00:36:45,270 --> 00:36:46,304
Thank you.

697
00:36:46,371 --> 00:36:48,239
Hurry, hurry. You'll get frostbite.

698
00:37:00,185 --> 00:37:03,054
Han-cheol, just how far are we going?

699
00:37:03,121 --> 00:37:05,323
We're here, we're here.

700
00:37:06,891 --> 00:37:08,359
This place is nice.

701
00:37:09,260 --> 00:37:12,897
Wow! This place is so nice.
It's perfect, just perfect!

702
00:37:17,836 --> 00:37:20,739
But why did we come here?

703
00:37:20,805 --> 00:37:22,240
And what is all this?

704
00:37:22,307 --> 00:37:25,276
Why else? We're here to do business.

705
00:37:25,343 --> 00:37:28,713
Business? What kind of business?

706
00:37:34,686 --> 00:37:35,987
Open it.

707
00:37:36,755 --> 00:37:38,590
Come on, open it.

708
00:37:51,169 --> 00:37:53,071
Huh? It's my portfolio.

709
00:37:53,905 --> 00:37:55,206
Why is this in here?

710
00:37:56,508 --> 00:37:58,676
I didn't mean for you to look at this.

711
00:37:59,444 --> 00:38:02,847
I meant what's in the box.
Look inside, right inside.

712
00:38:03,581 --> 00:38:04,749
Ta-da!

713
00:38:06,151 --> 00:38:07,051
It's clothes?

714
00:38:08,153 --> 00:38:10,588
But why do this with me…

715
00:38:14,325 --> 00:38:15,360
Huh?

716
00:38:16,327 --> 00:38:17,896
This… This is…

717
00:38:19,597 --> 00:38:23,935
Yes, that's right.
The clothes you designed yourself.

718
00:38:24,936 --> 00:38:29,040
Your dream is to be a designer
and launch your own brand, right?

719
00:38:29,107 --> 00:38:30,942
How did you know that…

720
00:38:31,009 --> 00:38:33,411
When you were sick not long ago,

721
00:38:33,478 --> 00:38:37,048
I was taking care of you
and happened to see your portfolio.

722
00:38:37,115 --> 00:38:39,484
Someone I know runs
a Seoul garment factory.

723
00:38:39,551 --> 00:38:41,452
So I asked them to make these.

724
00:38:41,519 --> 00:38:43,054
How do you like them?

725
00:38:43,121 --> 00:38:44,322
Han-cheol.

726
00:38:49,561 --> 00:38:51,729
You're much more talented
than I thought.

727
00:38:51,796 --> 00:38:53,331
The clothes are so pretty.

728
00:38:53,398 --> 00:38:56,534
They're even prettier made like this.

729
00:39:01,339 --> 00:39:03,308
They must take after their owner.

730
00:39:10,348 --> 00:39:11,816
YEON & CHEOL

731
00:39:11,883 --> 00:39:15,653
Huh? But what is this?

732
00:39:15,720 --> 00:39:18,990
That? It's the label, the brand label.

733
00:39:19,057 --> 00:39:22,994
It's "Su-yeon and Han-cheol,"
shortened to "Yeon & Cheol."

734
00:39:23,061 --> 00:39:27,232
I spent a week coming up with it.
Don't you like it?

735
00:39:30,535 --> 00:39:32,637
It's not bad.

736
00:39:32,704 --> 00:39:34,606
Right? Right?

737
00:39:35,473 --> 00:39:37,809
Shall we open for business, then?

738
00:39:41,246 --> 00:39:43,882
Wow, these clothes are so pretty.
Truly amazing!

739
00:40:09,908 --> 00:40:13,478
Come on, clothes for sale!
Clothes for sale, clothes for sale!

740
00:40:13,544 --> 00:40:16,381
-Everyone, clothes for sale!
-Clothes for sale!

741
00:40:16,447 --> 00:40:18,583
-Clothes for sale!
-Come take a look.

742
00:40:38,136 --> 00:40:41,339
Don't worry so much.
They say he's okay now.

743
00:40:41,406 --> 00:40:45,243
Okay, but are you all right?

744
00:40:45,310 --> 00:40:48,746
I'm fine. Still, I'm grateful to him.

745
00:40:48,813 --> 00:40:51,816
-For what?
-It's all thanks to him.

746
00:40:51,883 --> 00:40:54,686
Now I can talk to you face-to-face.

747
00:40:56,754 --> 00:41:00,758
Mi-yeong, let's stop
this exhausting nonsense now.

748
00:41:00,825 --> 00:41:03,861
Honestly, I really like you.

749
00:41:04,562 --> 00:41:06,064
Do you dislike me?

750
00:41:06,130 --> 00:41:08,199
Um… Well, that's…

751
00:41:08,266 --> 00:41:10,668
No explanations. Just answer me.

752
00:41:10,735 --> 00:41:11,703
Like me or hate me?

753
00:41:11,769 --> 00:41:13,338
I like you, but…

754
00:41:13,404 --> 00:41:15,573
That's enough. Come with me.

755
00:41:17,442 --> 00:41:19,644
You're doing great. Now put it in.

756
00:41:19,711 --> 00:41:21,145
-Here.
-Grab another leaf.

757
00:41:21,212 --> 00:41:25,583
If you put too much seasoning
in the cabbage, it can get salty.

758
00:41:25,650 --> 00:41:28,619
So add just enough and mix it in.

759
00:41:28,686 --> 00:41:30,355
Okay.

760
00:41:30,989 --> 00:41:32,724
Like this, Mother?

761
00:41:32,790 --> 00:41:36,227
My dear daughter-in-law,
there's nothing you can't do!

762
00:41:36,294 --> 00:41:37,962
Oh, you're too kind.

763
00:41:43,768 --> 00:41:45,169
Sang-deuk…

764
00:41:46,738 --> 00:41:48,840
-What's with you two?
-Mom.

765
00:41:48,906 --> 00:41:51,109
I'm going to start over with Mi-yeong.

766
00:41:51,743 --> 00:41:52,610
What?

767
00:41:52,677 --> 00:41:55,580
Sang-deuk, what are you talking about?

768
00:41:55,646 --> 00:41:58,282
I love Mi-yeong.
Please let us get married.

769
00:42:01,886 --> 00:42:03,187
Oh, my goodness!

770
00:42:03,254 --> 00:42:04,889
Mother! Mother!

771
00:42:04,956 --> 00:42:07,291
Mom! Mom, what's wrong with you?

772
00:42:07,358 --> 00:42:09,260
Please, wake up!

773
00:42:10,094 --> 00:42:12,930
I'm so sorry. I'm sorry, kids.

774
00:42:13,698 --> 00:42:15,166
Forget it.

775
00:42:15,233 --> 00:42:17,502
I'm really, truly sorry.

776
00:42:17,568 --> 00:42:19,303
I'll refund the activity fee.

777
00:42:19,370 --> 00:42:21,539
Could I ask for your understanding?

778
00:42:21,606 --> 00:42:23,241
We don't need it.

779
00:42:23,307 --> 00:42:25,109
We're too uncomfortable to stay.

780
00:42:25,176 --> 00:42:26,611
-Come on, kids.
-Come here.

781
00:42:26,677 --> 00:42:28,346
Are you really just leaving?

782
00:42:28,413 --> 00:42:29,447
Come on, let's go.

783
00:42:29,514 --> 00:42:31,816
-Unbelievable.
-Please at least take this.

784
00:42:34,619 --> 00:42:37,555
I can't take this anymore, seriously.

785
00:42:39,857 --> 00:42:41,159
Thank you.

786
00:42:41,225 --> 00:42:42,927
-Thank you.
-Thank you. Goodbye.

787
00:42:44,662 --> 00:42:46,564
-Welcome.
-How much is this?

788
00:42:46,631 --> 00:42:49,167
I'm sorry, we're closed now. Sorry.

789
00:42:49,233 --> 00:42:50,868
But this one's still left.

790
00:42:50,935 --> 00:42:53,171
This item is already reserved.

791
00:42:53,237 --> 00:42:55,907
I'm so sorry. Truly sorry.

792
00:42:56,908 --> 00:42:58,609
Han-cheol, what reservation?

793
00:42:58,676 --> 00:43:00,845
I'm going to buy this one.

794
00:43:01,646 --> 00:43:04,048
There, I've paid for it.

795
00:43:05,249 --> 00:43:08,119
And this is a gift for you.

796
00:43:08,186 --> 00:43:11,089
What? Why give this to me…

797
00:43:11,155 --> 00:43:14,725
For the clothes you designed yourself,

798
00:43:14,792 --> 00:43:16,894
I'm the first to buy and gift them,

799
00:43:16,961 --> 00:43:19,564
and the only one in the world, right?

800
00:43:19,630 --> 00:43:22,767
Then that means you…

801
00:43:22,834 --> 00:43:25,403
You could never… forget me, right?

802
00:43:29,841 --> 00:43:31,676
No, I shouldn't do this.

803
00:43:31,742 --> 00:43:33,978
Please forget me. Just forget me.

804
00:43:34,045 --> 00:43:36,180
Yes, please forget me.

805
00:43:37,648 --> 00:43:41,319
Um, Su-yeon…
Could you try this on just once?

806
00:43:44,622 --> 00:43:46,290
Please, just this once.

807
00:43:47,358 --> 00:43:48,226
All right.

808
00:43:48,292 --> 00:43:51,329
Thank you, thank you, Su-yeon.

809
00:43:59,770 --> 00:44:04,041
Wow, Su-yeon, the more I look,
the better it looks on you.

810
00:44:04,108 --> 00:44:07,578
Aren't you just designing clothes
that look good on you?

811
00:44:07,645 --> 00:44:09,780
-Um, Han-cheol.
-Yes?

812
00:44:10,648 --> 00:44:13,417
Thank you so much for today.

813
00:44:13,484 --> 00:44:17,455
Oh, don't mention it.
You're making me blush.

814
00:44:18,422 --> 00:44:19,657
I really mean it.

815
00:44:22,026 --> 00:44:25,229
Su-yeon, are you really that grateful?

816
00:44:26,964 --> 00:44:29,500
If you're that grateful…

817
00:44:30,701 --> 00:44:32,503
please grant me just one wish.

818
00:44:32,570 --> 00:44:35,606
Again? What is it this time?

819
00:44:41,913 --> 00:44:45,216
-What?
-No, no, no, never mind.

820
00:44:45,283 --> 00:44:46,651
It was just a joke.

821
00:44:46,717 --> 00:44:49,954
How could I ask you for that
unless I was out of my mind?

822
00:44:50,021 --> 00:44:51,322
It was just a joke.

823
00:44:51,389 --> 00:44:53,291
I… I should be going now.

824
00:44:53,357 --> 00:44:54,625
Get home safely.

825
00:44:56,194 --> 00:44:57,929
Um, Han-cheol.

826
00:44:59,430 --> 00:45:00,865
Yes?

827
00:45:14,879 --> 00:45:18,216
I… I only granted it
because you said it was your wish.

828
00:45:18,282 --> 00:45:20,318
Goodbye, then.

829
00:45:33,965 --> 00:45:34,899
I can die happy.

830
00:45:37,735 --> 00:45:40,304
Oh, cheer up, Yun-hui.

831
00:45:40,371 --> 00:45:42,873
The Rural Experience Village
can work next time.

832
00:45:42,940 --> 00:45:44,275
What next time?

833
00:45:44,342 --> 00:45:47,778
Our first guest left that upset.
There won't be a next time.

834
00:45:47,845 --> 00:45:49,614
It's completely ruined. Ruined.

835
00:45:49,680 --> 00:45:51,282
Anyway, though.

836
00:45:51,349 --> 00:45:53,417
By the way, Sang-deuk and Mi-yeong…

837
00:45:53,484 --> 00:45:55,519
when did they get together like that?

838
00:45:55,586 --> 00:45:56,988
I don't know either.

839
00:45:57,955 --> 00:46:00,091
I wonder if his mom is okay.

840
00:46:00,157 --> 00:46:02,460
I can't blame her for fainting.

841
00:46:04,562 --> 00:46:06,230
Mom, I'm sorry.

842
00:46:06,297 --> 00:46:09,734
But I really do love Mi-yeong.

843
00:46:10,401 --> 00:46:11,769
I really mean it.

844
00:46:11,836 --> 00:46:15,339
I know you don't like it,
but please trust me just this once.

845
00:46:15,406 --> 00:46:17,041
I promise we'll be so happy.

846
00:46:17,675 --> 00:46:19,677
Huh? Mom?

847
00:46:19,744 --> 00:46:22,046
Are you really going to be like this?

848
00:46:22,113 --> 00:46:23,214
All right, then.

849
00:46:23,281 --> 00:46:24,682
Until you allow it,

850
00:46:24,749 --> 00:46:27,952
I won't budge an inch from here,
just so you know.

851
00:46:38,596 --> 00:46:42,566
Anyway, the whole village
will be on edge again for a while.

852
00:46:43,401 --> 00:46:45,403
Who told them to stir up trouble?

853
00:46:49,807 --> 00:46:51,375
I'm home!

854
00:46:55,046 --> 00:46:57,415
-What's with you? What's this again?
-Ki-jun.

855
00:46:58,382 --> 00:47:00,851
The world is truly beautiful, man!

856
00:47:01,719 --> 00:47:04,855
That's gross, stop it! Let go! Go! Go!

857
00:47:07,858 --> 00:47:09,460
Yes, hello?

858
00:47:10,528 --> 00:47:12,630
Yes, Teacher. Hello, how are you?

859
00:47:13,831 --> 00:47:16,500
What? Min-ho didn't come to school?

860
00:47:19,303 --> 00:47:22,006
But he definitely left
for school this morning.

861
00:47:22,707 --> 00:47:25,076
Yes, I understand. Yes, okay.

862
00:47:25,843 --> 00:47:28,212
-Say what?
-They say Min-ho's not at school?

863
00:47:28,279 --> 00:47:31,649
Yes, I'm sure he left for school
this morning. This is strange.

864
00:47:31,716 --> 00:47:35,152
-Try calling him, Yun-hui.
-Uh… Right, right.

865
00:47:38,055 --> 00:47:39,523
The phone is powered off…

866
00:47:39,590 --> 00:47:42,326
Oh, no, his phone is turned off too.

867
00:47:42,393 --> 00:47:44,528
Oh, dear, what is this? What happened?

868
00:47:45,996 --> 00:47:47,898
Will you all just sit and worry?

869
00:47:47,965 --> 00:47:49,400
We should go out and look.

870
00:47:49,467 --> 00:47:50,968
Oh, right. Yes, okay.

871
00:47:51,669 --> 00:47:54,739
He'll be fine,
so don't worry and hurry outside.

872
00:47:56,040 --> 00:47:57,908
Come on, let's go, let's go!

873
00:47:58,943 --> 00:48:00,578
YEOUIDO

874
00:48:13,023 --> 00:48:15,559
-Excuse me, mister.
-Yes, what is it, kiddo?

875
00:48:16,360 --> 00:48:19,063
How do I get to this place?

876
00:48:22,199 --> 00:48:26,170
For this place, just go right
for about 50 meters over there.

877
00:48:26,237 --> 00:48:28,372
But did you come all by yourself?

878
00:48:33,677 --> 00:48:36,480
-Is he still… still not back?
-No. How did it go?

879
00:48:36,547 --> 00:48:38,048
We can't find him anywhere.

880
00:48:38,115 --> 00:48:39,283
Is he at a friend's?

881
00:48:39,350 --> 00:48:41,352
I checked all his friends' houses.

882
00:48:41,419 --> 00:48:43,120
Some must live in other areas.

883
00:48:43,187 --> 00:48:44,889
-Have their contacts?
-Contacts?

884
00:48:45,756 --> 00:48:47,491
I have their contacts, I do.

885
00:48:51,762 --> 00:48:53,097
Contacts, contacts.

886
00:48:53,164 --> 00:48:54,899
Contacts, contacts.

887
00:48:57,168 --> 00:49:00,271
Auntie, have you seen
the concert ticket that was here?

888
00:49:00,337 --> 00:49:02,273
Concert ticket? I didn't see that.

889
00:49:03,274 --> 00:49:04,875
Don't tell me…

890
00:49:08,712 --> 00:49:10,114
Min-ho, what's going on?

891
00:49:10,881 --> 00:49:13,017
And what are you doing at my desk?

892
00:49:13,784 --> 00:49:15,486
I'm just looking for an eraser.

893
00:49:15,553 --> 00:49:17,221
Oh, really?

894
00:49:19,690 --> 00:49:21,959
Um, what's today's date, by any chance?

895
00:49:22,026 --> 00:49:25,129
Uh, today… Today is the 13th.

896
00:49:25,196 --> 00:49:26,430
The 13th?

897
00:49:26,497 --> 00:49:29,366
Why are you so shocked?
What's special about today?

898
00:49:30,134 --> 00:49:34,338
Yun-hui, is today the concert
for that man called Min-ho's dad?

899
00:49:35,172 --> 00:49:36,540
What does that mean?

900
00:49:36,607 --> 00:49:38,776
So you mean Min-ho knows about his dad?

901
00:49:38,843 --> 00:49:40,077
I… I think he does.

902
00:49:40,144 --> 00:49:43,180
I can't just sit here.
I… I have to go to Seoul.

903
00:49:43,247 --> 00:49:45,649
Yun-hui, can you drive in this state?

904
00:49:45,716 --> 00:49:47,351
-I'll go with her.
-You go too.

905
00:49:47,418 --> 00:49:49,587
Yun-hui! Don't! Hey, Yun-hui!

906
00:49:51,188 --> 00:49:53,524
-Yu-na.
-Hyeok said he's going.

907
00:49:53,591 --> 00:49:55,659
No, but still…

908
00:50:05,870 --> 00:50:08,973
Could you drive a little faster?

909
00:50:09,039 --> 00:50:10,841
Okay, I will.

910
00:50:13,310 --> 00:50:16,680
Could Min-ho really know about his dad?

911
00:50:16,747 --> 00:50:18,249
Well, I'm not sure.

912
00:50:18,315 --> 00:50:21,719
But how on earth did he find that out?

913
00:50:21,785 --> 00:50:24,655
What if something happens to him?
This is terrible.

914
00:50:24,722 --> 00:50:27,224
I reported it to the police, okay?

915
00:50:27,291 --> 00:50:30,261
We don't know who might call,
so let's just wait, okay?

916
00:50:34,932 --> 00:50:36,634
Yu-na.

917
00:50:36,700 --> 00:50:38,435
-Yes?
-I mean about earlier.

918
00:50:40,771 --> 00:50:42,573
Why did you do that?

919
00:50:42,640 --> 00:50:44,041
Well… just because.

920
00:50:44,808 --> 00:50:48,512
I was just worried you'd crash
driving all worked up.

921
00:50:50,180 --> 00:50:52,349
I'm going inside to rest.

922
00:51:11,335 --> 00:51:12,770
Yu-na, we need to talk.

923
00:51:12,836 --> 00:51:13,938
I'm tired.

924
00:51:14,705 --> 00:51:17,708
Why are you acting like this?
What's the reason?

925
00:51:21,946 --> 00:51:24,949
Because you're going a bit too far.

926
00:51:25,616 --> 00:51:27,751
-How so?
-How you act toward Yun-hui.

927
00:51:27,818 --> 00:51:31,855
It goes way beyond mere sympathy
or pity for your first love.

928
00:51:33,824 --> 00:51:35,859
So it really bothers me.

929
00:51:35,926 --> 00:51:37,628
What are you talking about?

930
00:51:37,695 --> 00:51:39,563
So you're saying I like Yun-hui?

931
00:51:39,630 --> 00:51:42,633
Well, I wouldn't know about that.

932
00:51:42,700 --> 00:51:44,301
Stop talking nonsense.

933
00:51:44,368 --> 00:51:46,337
Why are you getting so mad?

934
00:51:46,403 --> 00:51:48,105
It just looks that way to me.

935
00:51:49,673 --> 00:51:51,308
I'm tired. Could you leave?

936
00:52:02,820 --> 00:52:06,924
LEE HYEON-SEOK PIANO RECITAL

937
00:52:13,464 --> 00:52:17,601
LEE HYEON-SEOK

938
00:52:22,840 --> 00:52:24,108
That was wonderful.

939
00:52:24,174 --> 00:52:25,576
-Isn't he so good?
-Yes.

940
00:52:25,643 --> 00:52:27,378
-I was amazed.
-Glad we came.

941
00:52:29,713 --> 00:52:32,383
Where are you going, kiddo?
The show is over.

942
00:52:32,449 --> 00:52:35,019
I just wanted to take a look inside.

943
00:52:35,085 --> 00:52:37,221
I… I left something behind.

944
00:52:39,023 --> 00:52:41,325
I even have a ticket right here.

945
00:52:45,229 --> 00:52:46,864
But come right back out.

946
00:52:46,930 --> 00:52:48,799
Yes, sir.

947
00:52:51,835 --> 00:52:53,504
LEE HYEON-SEOK PIANO RECITAL

948
00:52:55,072 --> 00:52:57,107
Min-ho!

949
00:52:57,174 --> 00:52:58,475
Min-ho!

950
00:53:01,645 --> 00:53:05,249
Hyeon-seok, you did great!
It was a huge hit, a massive hit!

951
00:53:05,315 --> 00:53:07,284
Fans were clamoring to see your face.

952
00:53:07,351 --> 00:53:09,953
I barely talked them into going home.

953
00:53:10,020 --> 00:53:10,988
See these flowers!

954
00:53:11,055 --> 00:53:13,891
There's a whole truckload more outside!

955
00:53:15,959 --> 00:53:17,828
Oh, and also,

956
00:53:17,895 --> 00:53:22,533
articles calling your concert a hit
are already all over the internet…

957
00:53:22,599 --> 00:53:25,636
Change and come out quick.
Time to party! Let's party!

958
00:53:25,703 --> 00:53:27,371
Okay, I'll change and come out.

959
00:53:43,053 --> 00:53:45,255
Hey, kiddo, you shouldn't be in here.

960
00:53:45,322 --> 00:53:48,692
Mister, are you Lee Hyeon-seok?

961
00:53:50,260 --> 00:53:51,261
Yes, I am.

962
00:53:54,832 --> 00:53:56,433
Why do you ask?

963
00:53:56,500 --> 00:53:57,901
Then…

964
00:53:59,269 --> 00:54:01,505
are you my dad?

965
00:54:02,639 --> 00:54:04,742
What? Dad?

966
00:54:05,609 --> 00:54:07,711
-Min-ho!
-Mom!

967
00:54:07,778 --> 00:54:09,246
Oh, where have you been?

968
00:54:09,313 --> 00:54:11,348
Do you know how worried I was?

969
00:54:11,415 --> 00:54:13,350
Oh, you little rascal, I swear!

970
00:54:13,417 --> 00:54:14,885
You little brat.

971
00:54:14,952 --> 00:54:16,386
Are you all right?

972
00:54:16,453 --> 00:54:19,423
Yun-hui, what are you doing here…

973
00:54:20,924 --> 00:54:22,926
Wait, you're his mom?

974
00:54:23,427 --> 00:54:24,828
You said you didn't marry.

975
00:54:27,097 --> 00:54:29,433
Uh, well, that's…

976
00:54:36,673 --> 00:54:39,576
You're okay, right? You're okay.

977
00:54:41,879 --> 00:54:43,547
It's all right.

978
00:54:47,050 --> 00:54:48,719
So…

979
00:54:49,386 --> 00:54:54,158
you're saying that child is my son?

980
00:54:59,396 --> 00:55:03,100
Then why, why didn't you tell me then?

981
00:55:05,235 --> 00:55:07,371
I had no other choice either.

982
00:55:08,605 --> 00:55:10,107
Being pregnant with Min-ho…

983
00:55:11,675 --> 00:55:13,310
I only knew after you left.

984
00:55:14,077 --> 00:55:17,748
What? Still, you should've told me!

985
00:55:20,184 --> 00:55:22,719
We'd broken up.
I didn't want to hold you back.

986
00:55:22,786 --> 00:55:25,022
How can you call that an excuse?

987
00:55:26,423 --> 00:55:27,291
I'm sorry.

988
00:55:27,357 --> 00:55:29,660
Is "I'm sorry" supposed to fix this?

989
00:55:32,696 --> 00:55:36,166
How could you do this to me? How?

990
00:55:38,569 --> 00:55:40,037
I'm so sorry.

991
00:55:42,105 --> 00:55:43,774
Hyeon-seok!

992
00:55:46,443 --> 00:55:48,078
What are you doing here?

993
00:55:48,712 --> 00:55:49,847
Jeong-eun.

994
00:55:49,913 --> 00:55:52,983
Your mom and dad won't stop
telling you to hurry inside.

995
00:55:53,050 --> 00:55:56,019
-Come on, let's go.
-Uh, sure, okay.

996
00:55:58,121 --> 00:56:01,058
-By the way, who is she?
-Uh…

997
00:56:01,124 --> 00:56:03,894
Um, this is…

998
00:56:04,995 --> 00:56:07,664
Oh, I'm a fan. Just a fan.

999
00:56:07,731 --> 00:56:09,800
I truly enjoyed your concert.

1000
00:56:15,105 --> 00:56:16,640
Let's go.

1001
00:56:19,509 --> 00:56:21,778
Okay, sure.

1002
00:56:49,506 --> 00:56:52,976
I'm sorry, Mom.

1003
00:56:54,511 --> 00:56:56,213
Let's go home.

1004
00:56:56,280 --> 00:56:58,282
We'll talk at home.

1005
00:57:21,571 --> 00:57:24,474
Why do you look so grim?
They found Min-ho.

1006
00:57:24,541 --> 00:57:26,443
No, it's nothing.

1007
00:57:31,281 --> 00:57:32,649
Min-ho!

1008
00:57:34,584 --> 00:57:37,287
Min-ho, what happened?

1009
00:57:37,854 --> 00:57:40,557
Aunt, I'm tired, so I'll go rest now.

1010
00:57:48,432 --> 00:57:50,834
What's going on here, huh?

1011
00:57:50,901 --> 00:57:52,235
I said, what happened?

1012
00:57:52,302 --> 00:57:54,905
Well, the thing is…

1013
00:58:00,610 --> 00:58:01,878
What's your reason?

1014
00:58:04,081 --> 00:58:07,517
I think you went a bit too far.

1015
00:58:07,584 --> 00:58:08,652
How so?

1016
00:58:10,053 --> 00:58:12,356
The way you acted toward Yun-hui.

1017
00:58:13,090 --> 00:58:16,727
It goes too far to be mere pity
or sympathy for your first love.

1018
00:58:17,394 --> 00:58:19,396
So it bothers me.

1019
00:58:19,463 --> 00:58:21,198
Of course. I knew it.

1020
00:58:21,264 --> 00:58:23,400
No way a successful guy has no woman.

1021
00:58:23,467 --> 00:58:25,702
Then why come here if he has a woman?

1022
00:58:25,769 --> 00:58:28,105
Hey, it's not his fault.

1023
00:58:28,171 --> 00:58:30,640
He didn't even know Min-ho existed.

1024
00:58:31,141 --> 00:58:33,043
For him, Yun-hui, and Min-ho,

1025
00:58:33,110 --> 00:58:34,911
fate is so tragic, truly tragic.

1026
00:58:34,978 --> 00:58:37,914
Anyway, I'm worried about Min-ho.

1027
00:58:37,981 --> 00:58:38,849
Is he okay?

1028
00:58:38,915 --> 00:58:40,817
I worry more for her than Min-ho.

1029
00:58:40,884 --> 00:58:41,985
She must be shocked.

1030
00:58:44,955 --> 00:58:46,189
Where are you going?

1031
00:58:46,256 --> 00:58:48,658
I feel stifled. Just getting some air.

1032
00:59:02,706 --> 00:59:05,942
I'm sorry, Mom.

1033
00:59:07,744 --> 00:59:12,749
I just wanted to see Dad's face.

1034
00:59:13,950 --> 00:59:18,188
I wondered what he looked like
and what kind of person he was.

1035
00:59:21,258 --> 00:59:25,228
Mom, I'm really sorry I upset you.

1036
00:59:26,463 --> 00:59:30,167
Don't be sorry.
I'm the one who should be sorry.

1037
00:59:31,535 --> 00:59:36,339
But I saw Dad's face now, so I'm okay.

1038
00:59:37,007 --> 00:59:40,010
Just having you is enough for me, Mom.

1039
00:59:42,079 --> 00:59:46,116
I'll never upset you again, Mom.

1040
